# BookReel environment — PLACEHOLDERS ONLY.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. `.env.local` is gitignored; this file is
# not, so never put a real value in here. No value below is a real credential.
#
# Everything in this file is OPTIONAL. With none of it set, BookReel runs
# exactly as it does today: the Publish Center reports REQUIRES_CONNECTION for
# every platform and the assisted handoff (download the video and the poster,
# copy the title, description and hashtags, open the platform's own uploader)
# works in full.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- database
# SQLite by default, resolved to prisma/dev.db when unset.
# DATABASE_URL="file:./prisma/dev.db"

# ------------------------------------------------- YouTube publishing (OAuth)
#
# WHAT THIS BUYS YOU: BookReel uploads the rendered video to your channel over
# the official YouTube Data API v3, as PRIVATE, and gives you a link into
# YouTube Studio to review and publish it yourself. Nothing here can make a
# video public.
#
# WHAT IT NEVER DOES: it never asks for, stores or transmits your Google
# password. You sign in on accounts.google.com, in your own browser. The API
# route does no automation of YouTube Studio (the OPTIONAL browser-window route
# further down is a separate, explicitly chosen alternative).
#
# WHAT TO DO IN GOOGLE CLOUD (console.cloud.google.com), once:
#
#  1. Create (or pick) a project.
#  2. APIs & Services -> Library -> enable "YouTube Data API v3".
#  3. APIs & Services -> OAuth consent screen:
#       - User type: External is fine for a personal channel.
#       - Add the scope https://www.googleapis.com/auth/youtube.upload
#       - Add the scope https://www.googleapis.com/auth/youtube.readonly (used
#         only to confirm WHICH channel is connected; see the note below)
#       - While the app is in "Testing", add the channel's Google account under
#         "Test users". Without this, consent is refused.
#  4. APIs & Services -> Credentials -> Create credentials -> OAuth client ID:
#       - Application type: Web application.
#       - Authorised redirect URIs: add EXACTLY the value you set for
#         GOOGLE_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI below. Character for character, including
#         the port and the absence of a trailing slash.
#  5. Copy the client ID and client secret into the two variables below.
#
# The client ID is public by design (it appears in the authorisation URL). The
# client SECRET is server-only: it is never sent to the browser, never logged,
# and never put in a response body.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID="000000000000-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx.apps.googleusercontent.com"
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET="replace-me-with-the-client-secret"

# The callback this app serves, and the value Google must have on file. It has
# to be an exact match or Google answers `redirect_uri_mismatch` on its own
# error page, after you have already signed in. There is deliberately no
# default: this app cannot know which host and port you registered.
#   local dev on the default port:  http://localhost:3000/api/publish/youtube/callback
#   this install (port 3013):       http://localhost:3013/api/publish/youtube/callback
#   behind a domain:                https://your.host/api/publish/youtube/callback
# GOOGLE_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI="http://localhost:3013/api/publish/youtube/callback"

# THE TOKEN-ENCRYPTION KEY. Required for any platform connection.
#
# Google's refresh token is a long-lived credential — it can mint upload access
# to your channel for months. It is stored AES-256-GCM encrypted with this key
# and never in plaintext, so a copied dev.db is not a copy of your channel.
#
# Generate one with:   openssl rand -base64 32
# Accepted: 32 random bytes as base64 or 64 hex characters (used verbatim), or
# a passphrase of at least 32 characters (scrypt-derived). Shorter is refused.
#
# CHANGING IT invalidates every stored connection: Disconnect and reconnect.
# LOSING IT is not a disaster — reconnecting re-grants access in one click.
# BOOKREEL_TOKEN_KEY="replace-me-with-32-random-bytes-base64"

# Which YouTube category uploads are filed under. 27 = Education (the default),
# 22 = People & Blogs. A book summary has no derivable category, so this is a
# documented default rather than a guess buried in a request body.
# YOUTUBE_CATEGORY_ID="27"

# Scopes the YouTube consent asks for: youtube.upload (to upload) and
# youtube.readonly (ONLY so this app can ask YouTube which channel it just
# connected, and refuse to publish to the wrong one). A connection made before
# youtube.readonly existed keeps uploading; the card asks you to reconnect to
# verify it.

# --------------------------------------------- Instagram publishing (Meta API)
#
# WHAT THIS BUYS YOU: BookReel posts a Reel to your Instagram professional
# account over Meta's official Graph API (Content Publishing). It does NOT use
# your Instagram password and does not automate any website (the OPTIONAL
# browser-window route further down is a separate, explicitly chosen alternative).
#
# IT POSTS PUBLICLY AND AT ONCE. Instagram's API has no draft or private mode, so
# the Publish Center asks you to confirm before it sends anything.
#
# WHAT YOU NEED, once:
#
#  1. An Instagram Business or Creator account, linked to a Facebook Page.
#  2. A Meta app (developers.facebook.com) with the "Facebook Login" product and
#     the Instagram permissions below. Valid OAuth Redirect URI, EXACTLY:
#         <PUBLIC_BASE_URL>/api/publish/instagram/callback
#     Permissions: instagram_basic, instagram_content_publish, pages_show_list,
#     pages_read_engagement, business_management. Until Meta App Review approves
#     instagram_content_publish for the app, it works only for accounts holding a
#     role on the app (Administrator / Developer / Tester).
#  3. A PUBLIC https address for this server. Instagram does not accept an
#     upload: it FETCHES the video from PUBLIC_BASE_URL itself, through a signed
#     link that expires in minutes. http://localhost cannot work for publishing.
#
# META_APP_SECRET is server-only: never sent to the browser, never logged.
# META_APP_ID="000000000000000"
# META_APP_SECRET="replace-me-with-the-app-secret"
# PUBLIC_BASE_URL="https://your.public.host"
# Optional: the Graph API version (default v21.0).
# META_GRAPH_VERSION="v21.0"

# WHICH ACCOUNTS THIS INSTALL PUBLISHES TO. After you connect, each platform's own
# API is asked which account the credential belongs to, and publishing is blocked
# unless it is the one named here (case-insensitive, leading @ optional). A label
# or a channel title is never trusted. These are the defaults:
# BOOKREEL_YOUTUBE_HANDLE="@betweenpages08-l4d"
# BOOKREEL_INSTAGRAM_HANDLE="@between_pages"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- narration
# Optional third-party voices. Pocket (local) needs no key and is the default.
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY="replace-me"
# OPENAI_API_KEY="replace-me"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- sign-in
# Set to "false" only when terminating TLS in front of the app on plain http.
# AUTH_COOKIE_SECURE="true"

# ------------------------------------- OPTIONAL: publish via a browser window
#
# An alternative to the two API routes above, for an install with no Google
# project or Meta app. It is chosen per publish ("Publish via browser window" in
# the Publish Center) and is never used unless you pick it. The official APIs
# stay the recommended route: this one drives a website, which can break when the
# site changes and which the platform's terms may not welcome.
#
# WHAT HAPPENS: a real Chromium window opens on the computer running BookReel.
# The first time, you sign in to YouTube / Instagram IN THAT WINDOW and clear any
# security check yourself. BookReel never types your password, never solves a
# CAPTCHA or two-step prompt, and never tries to get past one: if a sign-in or a
# check appears the job stops (status "Needs you"), the window stays open, and you
# press Retry once you have dealt with it. The sign-in is kept in a Chromium
# profile under <work root>/browser-profiles/<platform> (one per platform, created
# empty); BookReel never reads or copies it.
#
# A job interrupted by a restart is NEVER re-run automatically: its outcome is
# unknown, so it is handed to you ("Needs you") to check the platform first.
#
# Chromium is the one Playwright installs (`npx playwright-core install chromium`).
# Set to "1" to hide the window. A hidden window cannot be signed in to, so use it
# only once the profile is already signed in; leave unset to sign in.
# BOOKREEL_PUBLISH_HEADLESS="1"
